Upstream behavior:
  OneConnect Bridge emulates a Huawei OneConnect parent gateway and maps Home
  Assistant entities into Huawei Smart Life as virtual child devices
  (Home Assistant -> Huawei).

Behavior of this derivative work:
  This project keeps the upstream behavior: it emulates a Huawei gateway, maps
  Home Assistant entities into Huawei Smart Life as virtual child devices, and
  keeps them in sync (Home Assistant -> Huawei).

Changes made in this derivative work:
  - Renamed the integration domain from "oneconnect_bridge" to
    "huawei_virtual_bridge" (manifest.json, const.py, config flow,
    strings.json, translations, and thread/log identifiers).
  - Rebranded user-facing text from "OneConnect Bridge" to
    "Huawei Virtual Bridge".
  - Added HACS/Marketplace packaging: hacs.json, LICENSE (Apache-2.0, copied
    from the upstream project), NOTICE, GitHub Actions workflows, English
    translations (translations/en.json) and this README.
  - Merged the child-device editor from OneConnect Bridge GUI
    (https://github.com/wang-peak/ha-oneconnect-bridge-gui) into the
    integration's options flow (child_ui/ package): product templates, device
    Profile parsing, per-service HA entity binding, contract editing, raw YAML
    editing, .bak backups, enable/disable and reload. The editor reads and
    writes this integration's own mapping.yaml only.
  - Business logic, the communication stack and default_mapping.yaml are
    unchanged. The adapter set is extended beyond the upstream one; the
    services and aliases supported by this project are documented in the
    README.

Files under custom_components/huawei_virtual_bridge/ are derived from the
corresponding files in OneConnect Bridge.

